import LeanFlagAlgebras.Core.Compute.Mask3

/-! # Order-7 certificate data: six-vertex completeness witnesses

Machine-generated witness tables for the canonicalization sweep: for
every tetrahedron-free 20-bit mask, the index of a vertex permutation
mapping it onto a listed representative. `w6Perms` packs the 720
permutations of six vertices in lexicographic order, three bits per
entry; `w6Chunks` packs one 10-bit permutation index per mask (sentinel
`1023` on non-tetrahedron-free positions), 1024 masks per chunk, in a
32 x 32 two-level listing indexed by the mask's high bits.

The tables carry no trusted content: the completeness sweep re-derives
every claim by kernel computation (bit-correspondence `decide` per mask
against the reconstructed image, membership by list scan), so a corrupt
entry can only make the sweep fail, never prove something false. -/

